{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":119646,"name":"User7431296185","username":"user7431296185","avatar_template":"/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/u/c68b51/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-10-10T16:34:47.283Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHello everyone,\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI’m experiencing a recurring printing issue with my \u003cstrong\u003eCreality Halot Mage S 14K\u003c/strong\u003e, and I’d like to know if anyone else has encountered the same problem.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAs you can see in the photos, \u003cstrong\u003eone part of the model prints perfectly, with all the details clearly reproduced, while the opposite side shows significant defects\u003c/strong\u003e: incomplete printing, deformations, and areas where the resin doesn’t seem to have cured properly.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis issue occurs with different models and \u003cstrong\u003etwo different resins\u003c/strong\u003e:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eFast Cast SuperCast (pink)\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eLiqcreate Wax Castable (blue)\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI’ve already tried several prints, adjusting the exposure settings, model orientation, and support configurations, but haven’t been able to solve the problem.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe printer is properly leveled, the workshop temperature is around 22°C (72°F), and the UV screen appears to be working correctly.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhat puzzles me most is that \u003cstrong\u003etwo opposite areas of the same model, printed simultaneously, show completely different results\u003c/strong\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHas anyone experienced this issue, particularly with this printer? Do you have any idea what might be causing it (UV screen, vat film, exposure settings, peeling forces, or something else)?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAnd most importantly, \u003cstrong\u003ehas anyone found a solution?\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThanks in advance for your help and advice!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv data-theme-tiles=\"1\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv data-theme-tiles=\"1\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/div\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":3,"updated_at":"2026-10-10T16:34:47.283Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":7,"reads":3,"readers_count":2,"score":50.6,"yours":false,"topic_id":54102,"topic_slug":"printing-issue-with-creality-halot-mage-s-14k-one-side-prints-perfectly-the-other-doesn-t","display_username":"User7431296185","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":1}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":43909,"hidden":false,"trust_level":0,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"mentioned_users":[],"post_url":"/t/printing-issue-with-creality-halot-mage-s-14k-one-side-prints-perfectly-the-other-doesn-t/54102/1","can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null,"can_vote":false},{"id":120260,"name":"Ignacio Grodek","username":"ShawarmaBaby","avatar_template":"/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/s/cdc98d/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-10-26T11:19:30.136Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003efrom all the things im reading right now (i have the same issue) people have sanded the plate and have succesfully found a solution for this. Thinking about doint it, because i get a perfect print from one side but nothing from the other (models stuck in fep from the begining)\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":2,"post_type":1,"posts_count":3,"updated_at":"2